-- title:
--   The rounds and final scans of the filtering host at σ = 0.0336175 write the all-edges flags
-- statement:
--   Let procedure $p_O$ of $P_0$ solve `Light.Filter2.oracleTask` with time $T_o$ and need $\nu_o$, let the core body `coreBody pRound pFinal`, the round body, the procedures of a round (`RoundProcs`) and of the final answer (`FinalProcs`) be in place in $P_0\mathbin{+\!\!+}R$, let `Env` hold for the all-edges instance $x$ ($n$ vertices, weight bound $U$) with first memory $\mu_0$ and free pointer $f$, and let $\mu$ satisfy `FMem` with all candidates active and no pair done. Then the core procedure, called at depth $d\le d_0+1$ with `coreArgs x fr`, returns within `tCore To n U` steps with the all-edges flags `aeFlags n AB BC AC` at `x.out` (for each pair $(a,b)$, whether some $c$ has $w(a,b)+w(b,c)+w(a,c)=0$), and every other cell below $f$ as in $\mu_0$ (`KeptBut`).
--
--   This is the filtering host of Lemma 3.1 (rounds of prime moduli from a pool in $[R,2R)$ that certify pairs and shrink the active candidates, then the final check), at the block size $s=2^{\lfloor0.0336175k\rfloor}$ of the 2.995561 parameters.
--
--   `Meets lim P p d args μ T Q` means: the call of procedure $p$ of $P$ at depth $d$ with the arguments `args` on memory $\mu$ returns within $T$ steps, under the limits `lim`, with a result $r$ and memory $\mu'$ satisfying $Q\,r\,\mu'$.
